  "modes": {
    "song": {
      "label": "Composed",
      "description": "Writes the melody and chords as an ABC score, then sings it; the job's `text` is that score, to edit and sing again with `score`.",
      "workflow": "song"
    },
    "free": {
      "label": "Unplanned",
      "description": "Sings straight from style and lyrics with no score: a little faster, looser in structure.",
      "workflow": "free"
    },
    "score": {
      "label": "From a score",
      "description": "Sings the ABC score given as `params.score` (one a song or cover take returned, edited or not): keep a tune, change its style, words or notes.",
      "workflow": "score",
      "required": [
        "score"
      ]
    },
    "cover": {
      "label": "Cover",
      "description": "Transcribes the melody of `audio` (SheetSage2) and sings it in a new style with new lyrics; the job's `text` is the transcribed score.",
      "workflow": "cover",
      "required": [
        "audio"
      ],
      "defaults": {
        "plan": "melody"
      }
    }
  },
  "default_mode": "song",
  "tiers": [
    "16gb",
    "24gb-64ram",
    "32gb",
    "48gb",
    "96gb"
  ],
  "notes": "From Comfy-Org's templates (audio_yue2_text2music, audio_yue2_music_cover), native nodes in the pinned ComfyUI. The templates load the int8 checkpoint (3.96 GB); bf16 runs on every tier (the reference pipeline peaks at 11-14 GB of VRAM), so the recipe uses it rather than a quantised build. Library LoRAs patch the music model only; a YuE2 LoRA's planner half is not applied."
}
